I think that Dave's idea of a wishing tree is an _excellent_ idea. - and don't 
be in too much of a hurry to fill the leaves with useless and cursed item's
either. Those people who are always griping about there being too many wishes
in nethack make me wonder if they have the easy option installed or something -
they are few and far between when I play. Furthermore a wish will give you
but a single item (up to three copies), and there is no single item so 
powerful that this unbalances the game. When I finally get a wish I can imagine
nothing more frustrating than being tricked out of getting anything useful
out of it. 

- you wished for a blessed +3 war hammer named Mjollnir (more)-
- the gods have decided to grant you (more)-
- a cursed -2 rubber duck named Sam

My pet peeve with nethack is that there is so much in the game that it is
absolutely impossible to figure out by yourself. If I hadn't been reading
this group I wonder if there is any way I would ever have guessed that 
dropping rings down sinks could be useful, or that engraving the word
Elbereth would be anything other than a waste of time. Oh sure there are the
rumours, but frankly I didn't find them much help. There are too many, they
are too cryptic, and are too hard to get in the game. Even when I cheated
somewhat ( cat rumor.file ) and just read all the rumours at one sitting, 
frankly they were not much help. Someone has asked if anyone has ever won 
without cheating by backing up save files. I think a much more interesting
question is how many people have won without first obtaining information from
some other source than merely playing the game. How many of you nethack
experts do NOT delve into the code to ferret out secrets, experiment in 
wizard or debug mode, exchange cheat sheets with other hackers, list the
rumor file, etc. At least Daves tree idea removes some of the advantage of this
kind of information. As things now stand, it is absolutely impossible for a
non-expert player to use a wish effectively. If you have never managed to get 
past level 10 (except for that time you accidentally teleported to level 29
and were killed by a hell-hound pup) how are you going to know to wish
for a blessed +3 war hammer named Mjollnir, or a suit of blessed +3 gray
dragon scale mail. At least with a tree, the beginners have a fighting chance.

